In article <nwang.759028681@black.clarku.edu>,\
 nwang@black.clarku.edu (Sysadmin) writes...
> I am trying to compile Nethack 3.1.3 in my Ultrix 4.2 account here.  I
> did everything but I need to edit the "Makefile" in the top directory.
> There are some things I couldn't quite understand:
>  GAME     = nethack
>  GAMEUID  = games
>  GAMEGRP  = bin
> I suspect these are for the people who wants to become Nethack admins at
> their sites?  However I just want to enjoy it myself(hehehehe :-), so
> should I comment them out?

     Leave "GAME" alone; there's no need to fiddle with it. Change
"GAMEUID" to your own username and "GAMEGRP" to your group (or primary
group if you're in more than one). Then you can leave all the setup
commands alone (although you might want to make the permissions more
restrictive after finishing the installation, but that isn't essential).
`make' may warn about some "chown" commands, but you can ignore those
because it's just trying to explicitly set the ownership to your own
account (assuming you change GAMEUID to match your ID, that is).

> Then comes what I think is the file permission stuff.  After that is:
>  GAMEDIR   = /usr/games/lib/$(GAME)dir
>  SHELLDIR  = /usr/games
> I take it from the comment in "Makefile" that $(GAME)dir is the same as
> HACKDIR in config.h?  But what is SHELLDIR?  Could someone please
> explain it to me?  By the way, I changed HACKDIR from the default to my
> personal nethack directory(/usr/users/nwang/nh).  So should I do the
> same with GAMEDIR?

     GAMEDIR should match HACKDIR; they both refer to the "playground"
directory where the compiled program and all its data files reside.
SHELLDIR is where `make install' will place a short shell script which
can be used to invoke the program.  SHELLDIR must be _different_ from
GAMEDIR/HACKDIR, because the script has the same file name as the
compiled program (ie, they're both named "nethack" so they can't be
in the same directory; whichever one got put in second would clobber
the first.).  The script isn't required to run the game, but since it's
the default setup you probably ought to use it.

     Don't set GAMEDIR to be the top level of your nethack source
tree, nor to any other existing directory whose contents you want to
keep.  `make install' removes all files from the target directory
prior to copying the program and data there.  SHELLDIR can be any
directory other than GAMEDIR; only one tiny file gets copied there
and any existing contents--other than "nethack"--won't be affected.



